menu "Matter"

    config MINIHUB_MATTER_ADAPTER
        bool "Enable Matter adapter / commissioner"
        default n

    config MINIHUB_MATTER_THREAD_VIA_BLE_COMMISSION
        bool "Commission new Thread devices over BLE"
        depends on MINIHUB_MATTER_ADAPTER
        depends on MINIHUB_THREAD_ADAPTER
        default y
        help
            First-time Thread join: BLE scan plus injecting this Hub's Thread
            operational dataset (discovery ble_thread). Turn off to keep
            Matter-over-Thread on-network commissioning (discovery network)
            and skip the BLE controller scan. Wi-Fi and Ethernet BLE
            commissioning are unchanged.

    config MINIHUB_MATTER_MAX_NODES
        int "Max Matter nodes tracked (device / subscription / identity tables)"
        default 128
        range 16 1024
        depends on MINIHUB_MATTER_ADAPTER
        help
            Hard safety cap for the Matter device, subscription and identity
            tables. The tables are heap-allocated from PSRAM at init; raising
            it costs PSRAM, lowering it rejects extra devices with a log line
            instead of silently dropping them.

    config MINIHUB_MATTER_COMMISSION_WAIT_MS
        int "Commission watchdog timeout (ms)"
        default 300000
        range 60000 900000
        depends on MINIHUB_MATTER_ADAPTER
        help
            How long minihub_matter_commission_wait() blocks waiting for a
            commission to finish before the watchdog declares "commission
            timed out". Operational DNS-SD (resolving the joined device on the
            Thread/ethernet fabric) can be slow on first browse — the local
            OTBR record may not be visible immediately after commissioning —
            so give it headroom beyond the previous 180 s. Raise this if a
            slow fabric still trips the watchdog; lower it for faster test
            feedback.

endmenu
